# Development Environment & Tooling

## Node.js Environment Setup
- **Node.js Version**: 24+ required (specified in [package.json](mdc:package.json) engines and [.nvmrc](mdc:.nvmrc))
- **Package Manager**: pnpm (lockfile: [pnpm-lock.yaml](mdc:pnpm-lock.yaml)); enable Corepack (`corepack enable`) to use the version from `packageManager` in [package.json](mdc:package.json)
- **Environment Variables**: Loaded from `.env`, `.env.local`, etc. by Next.js at build and runtime (see [Next.js env docs](https://nextjs.org/docs/app/guides/environment-variables))

### Environment Commands
```bash
# Use correct Node.js version
nvm use

# Install dependencies
pnpm install

# Development server with Turbopack
pnpm dev

# Build for production
pnpm build

# Start production server
pnpm start

# Linting
pnpm lint

# Docker build
pnpm build:docker
```

## Project Scripts and Commands

### Development Workflow
```bash
# Start development server with debugger and Turbopack
NODE_OPTIONS='--inspect' next dev --turbopack

# Build optimized production bundle
next build

# Start production server on port 8080
next start -p 8080

# Run ESLint (flat config: eslint.config.mjs)
pnpm lint

# Docker build for linux/amd64
docker build --platform linux/amd64 -t ghcr.io/conduitplatform/conduit-ui:latest .
```

### Git Workflow
```bash
# Install git hooks (runs `husky` from package.json prepare script)
pnpm prepare

# Generate changelog and tag release
pnpm release

# Commit with conventional format (via commitizen)
npx cz
```

